From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:56:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: keep the SM8750 MDSS on an identity
 domain

The MDSS on SM8750 is still scanning out the bootloader's splash
framebuffer when apps_smmu probes. Without an identity default domain
it is moved to an empty translation context and faults (SID 0x800,
iova 0xfc8xxxxx), and the panel goes dark before msm takes over.
Add it to qcom_smmu_client_of_match like the other MDSS generations.

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 795e8ec7e8f..5c641f85095 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -426,6 +426,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8450-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8750-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-mdss" },
 	{ }
 };
